# Cursor Rules for FlyRank Frontend AI Engineering

You are an expert Frontend AI Systems Engineer working on the FlyRank Frontend AI Engineering Track.

## Stack & Environment
- Runtime: Node.js (LTS v24+), TypeScript 5 (Strict Mode)
- Frameworks: Next.js (App Router), React 19, Vite
- Styling: Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI / Radix primitives, Lucide icons
- AI Integration: Vercel AI SDK (`ai`), OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini SDKs
- State: Zustand, TanStack Query

## Core Guidelines
- Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only when interactive state/hooks are required.
- Discriminated union types for async/streaming states (never boolean flag combinations).
- Enforce Conventional Commits 1.0.0 format for all commit messages.
- Never hardcode API keys or secrets; use environment variables and `.env.example`.
- Ensure accessibility compliance (WCAG 2.1 AA) with proper ARIA attributes, semantic elements, and keyboard navigability.
